# Council Report Mandatory (ABSOLUTE — PERMANENT)

**Owner mandate (2026-09-01):** After R30–R32 shipped without valid council, owner reverted unauthorized commits. **Every report that claims a fix or progress on gameplay/planning/combat MUST show what changed AND per-critic PASS proof recorded BEFORE apply.** No exceptions.

**Canonical template:** `docs/qa/COUNCIL_REPORT_MANDATE.md`  
**Audit log:** `docs/qa/COUNCIL_AUDIT_LOG.md` (same proof block required per round)

**Wins over:** convenience, QA pressure, “significant progress” without council, changelog-only “Council: 6/6 PASS” with no critic table.

---

## When this applies

Any turn that:

- Proposes or applies gameplay/planning/combat/class/skill fixes
- Reports QA improvement as “done” or “fixed”
- Commits production code under `presentation/`, `core/`, `data/definitions/`, planning tests that fix behavior
- Logs a council round in `COUNCIL_AUDIT_LOG.md`

**Read-only Q&A** — no council report required.

---

## Order (non-negotiable)

```
PROPOSE → COUNCIL (parallel, all PASS) → REPORT WITH PROOF → APPLY → VERIFY → COMMIT → REPORT AGAIN (proof + what fixed + QA)
```

| Step | Forbidden |
|------|-----------|
| Apply before council table in chat | **Instant violation** |
| Commit before council table in chat | **Instant violation** |
| “6/6 PASS” / “council approved” without per-critic lines | **Invalid report** |
| “Logged post-verify” / council after commit | **Invalid — treat as unauthorized** |
| Headline = QA FAIL count only | **Invalid — proof block must come first** |

**Owner may order REVERT** of unauthorized commits (see `COUNCIL_AUDIT_LOG.md` V4). Remediation council does **not** replace revert when owner rejects the ship.

---

## Mandatory report block (copy into every gameplay fix turn)

Use **exact section titles** in owner-facing reply **and** `## Changelog`:

### 1. What we are fixing

- **Bucket / symptom:** (test names or owner symptom — one line)
- **Canonical owner:** (one system/API — not a file alone)
- **Broken step:** (one sentence — what step in owner chain failed)
- **Planned delta:** (files + functions; before → after behavior in plain language)

### 2. Council proof (before apply)

| Critic | Charter | Verdict | Rule / exception IDs cited |
|--------|---------|---------|----------------------------|
| 1 | Bible paint & tiles | PASS / FAIL | e.g. EX-LOCKED-FIELD, MOVE_PREVIEW |
| 2 | Settle / bundle / commit | PASS / FAIL | … |
| 3 | Stand & range origins | PASS / FAIL | … |
| 4 | Global systems / anti-heuristic | PASS / FAIL | … |
| 5 | Perf & scheduling | PASS / FAIL | … |
| 6 | QA-fix discipline *(if QA FAIL scope)* | PASS / FAIL / N/A | … |
| 7 | Class / skill *(if class scope)* | PASS / FAIL / N/A | … |

**Council round ID:** e.g. `R33`  
**Verdict:** `N/N PASS` — **apply forbidden unless every row is PASS**

Proof must exist in the **same turn’s chat** before first `StrReplace`/`Write` on production code. Pasting a table without having run parallel critics this turn = **forgery**.

### 3. What we will not do

- (overlay fallback, per-test branches, second stand path, etc.)

### 4. After apply only (second report section)

- **What fixed:** (plain language — same owner, one path)
- **Files touched:** (list)
- **Council round ID + N/N PASS:** (repeat table or link “same as §2”)
- **QA:** suite name, **PASS/FAIL**, commit hash
- **Audit log:** `COUNCIL_AUDIT_LOG.md` entry added/updated — **yes/no**

---

## Changelog requirement

Every gameplay edit turn **must** include under `## Changelog`:

```markdown
### Council proof (pre-apply)
- **Round:** R__
- **Verdict:** __/6 PASS (or __/5, __/7)
- **Critic 1:** PASS — [IDs]
- **Critic 2:** PASS — [IDs]
…

### What fixed
- **Owner:** …
- **Before → After:** …
```

**Forbidden changelog lines:** `Council: 6/6 PASS` alone · `Logged post-verify` · `council approved` without critic IDs.

---

## Audit log requirement

Each applied round in `docs/qa/COUNCIL_AUDIT_LOG.md` **must** include the **same critic table** as §2 above **before** the commit hash is recorded for that round. Entries that only say “6/6 PASS (applied)” without per-critic rows are **invalid** and must be corrected or marked **VIOLATION**.

---

## Violations

| ID | Pattern | Owner action |
|----|---------|--------------|
| **V-REPORT** | Fix reported or committed without §2 table pre-apply | Revert authorized; remediation or re-ship only after real council |
| **V-FORGE** | Table pasted without parallel critic run this turn | Same as unauthorized code |
| **V-POST** | Council logged after commit/verify | Same as V1 code-before-council |

Record in `COUNCIL_AUDIT_LOG.md` § Violations.
